{"acceptance_length": 6.25, "acceptance_lengths": [8, 3, 8, 6, 8, 5, 3, 1, 4, 8, 5, 8, 8, 8, 3, 8, 7, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 6, 4, 1, 3, 8, 1, 5, 8, 8, 8, 5, 8, 8, 7, 5, 8, 8, 8, 8, 5, 4, 5, 8, 4, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 2, 8, 8, 8, 3, 8, 5, 1], "accepted_draft_lengths": [7, 2, 7, 5, 7, 4, 2, 0, 3, 7, 4, 7, 7, 7, 2, 7, 6, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 5, 3, 0, 2, 7, 0, 4, 7, 7, 7, 4, 7, 7, 6, 4, 7, 7, 7, 7, 4, 3, 4, 7, 3, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 1, 7, 7, 7, 2, 7, 4, 1], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 22960477184, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 22960459264, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "Let's break this down step by step to find the total cost to fill the pool.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Calculate the volume of the pool**\n\nThe pool is a **rectangular prism**, so the volume is calculated as:\n\n$$\n\\text{Volume} = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} \\times \\text{depth}\n$$\n\nGiven:\n- Length = 25 feet  \n- Width = 14 feet  \n- Depth = 4 feet  \n\n$$\n\\text{Volume} = 25 \\times 14 \\times 4 = 1400 \\text{ cubic feet}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Convert cubic feet to gallons**\n\nWe are told to **multiply the volume by 5.9** to get the number of gallons needed.\n\n$$\n\\text{Gallons} = 1400 \\times 5.9\n$$\n\nLet\u2019s calculate that:\n\n$$\n1400 \\times 5.9 = 1400 \\times (6 - 0.1) = 1400 \\times 6 - 1400 \\times 0.1 = 8400 - 140 = 8260\n$$\n\nSo, the pool requires **8260 gallons** of water.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Calculate the cost**\n\nThe cost is **$0.10 per gallon**.\n\n$$\n\\text{Cost} = 8260 \\times 0.10 = 826 \\text{ dollars}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 **Final Answer:**\n\n$$\n\\boxed{826}\n$$\n\nThe cost to fill the pool is **$826**.", "decode_seconds": 3.3433197028934956, "draft_calls": 60, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 136, "method": "native_target_eagle3", "output_hash": "d17a25e9a8a2c1057a00ed0b6ced2f2189df282881a34a4c4b2a113ad77c68b2", "output_tokens": 376, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23141594112, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23305650176, "problem_id": "gsm8k/