{"acceptance_length": 7.2272727272727275, "acceptance_lengths": [8, 8, 3, 8, 5, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 6, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 5, 1, 8, 8, 8, 8, 6, 2, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 3, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 7], "accepted_draft_lengths": [7, 7, 2, 7, 4, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 5, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 4, 0, 7, 7, 7, 7, 5, 1, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 2, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 22960476160, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 22960458752, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "We are given the following information:\n\n- Total number of plants = **100**\n- **One-fourth** of the plants are **indoor plants**.\n- **Two-thirds** of the **remaining** plants are **outdoor plants**.\n- The **rest** are **flowering plants**.\n- We are to find the **percent** of the plants that are **flowering plants**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Find the number of indoor plants\n\n$$\n\\text{Indoor plants} = \\frac{1}{4} \\times 100 = 25\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find the number of remaining plants after removing indoor plants\n\n$$\n\\text{Remaining plants} = 100 - 25 = 75\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Find the number of outdoor plants\n\n$$\n\\text{Outdoor plants} = \\frac{2}{3} \\times 75 = 50\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Find the number of flowering plants\n\n$$\n\\text{Flowering plants} = 75 - 50 = 25\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Find the percentage of flowering plants\n\n$$\n\\text{Percentage of flowering plants} = \\left( \\frac{25}{100} \\right) \\times 100 = 25\\%\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{25\\%}\n$$", "decode_seconds": 2.4725806461647153, "draft_calls": 44, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 75, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "4bca12596cde37b82da0567724939a4bcfb9a0c81eb0abfcbd264f6d37c89e34", "method": "relay_base", "output_hash": "8c75830c36ae419d841cb6c26ae1f978a6b1dba223e4cac41886331066451eb6", "output_tokens": 319, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23068509696, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23305650176, "problem_id": "gsm8k/fc290e5920b76571", "profile_regions